## Summary

The business-day rule for registration dates now extends to public holidays.

**Change** — `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:

The controller's `toBusinessDay(...)` previously only rolled Saturdays and Sundays forward to the next weekday. I added the fixed public-holiday list and made the roll-forward loop skip holidays as well, so an adjusted date landing on a listed holiday advances to the next non-holiday business day (a holiday adjacent to a weekend chains correctly through both):

```java
/** Fixed public holidays the business-day roll skips. */
private static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
    LocalDate.parse("2026-01-01"), LocalDate.parse("2026-01-26"),
    LocalDate.parse("2026-04-25"), LocalDate.parse("2026-12-25"),
    LocalDate.parse("2026-12-28"));

private static LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
    while (date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY
        || date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY
        || HOLIDAYS.contains(date)) {
        date = date.plusDays(1);
    }
    return date;
